  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Upper Reading (UPREAD) Activity</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">(Malawi):  The Upper Primary Reading (UPRead) activity will improve the reading and writing skills of  Standards 5-8 learners by developing quality and relevant Chichewa and English instructional and supplementary reading materials. UPRead will prepare learners to &quot;read to learn&quot;, excel in Primary School Leaving Certificate of Education examinations, and to be literate for life. The activity will strengthen the institutional capacity of the Malawi Institute of Education to manage and sustain a comprehensive instructional materials development system under Malawi&apos;s NRP. UPRead will support Malawi Institute of Education in the areas of: technical capacity for the curriculum development and design process, operational capacity for sustainability, and development of quality and relevant instructional and supplementary materials for upper primary English and Chichewa..UPRead will develop the following materials: Standards 5-8 English and Chichewa scope and sequence, learners&apos; books, teachers&apos; guides, supplementary readers, a supplementary resource guide, a continuous assessment and remediation manual, and syllabi. These materials will have an extensive reach, covering all the 34 education districts in Malawi and targeting 5,641 public primary schools, benefitting over 32,000 teachers and 1,819,596 Standards 5 to 8 learners.  .UPRead supports the U.S. government&apos;s Basic Education Strategy, underscoring the importance of equal access to relevant, quality education; and the ICS Mission Objective 3.3 - Malawi expands educational opportunity to equip its citizens with foundational and marketable skills responsive to Malawi&apos;s public and private sector needs. UPRead supports the Mission&apos;s Strategy through endeavouring to strengthen capacities of the Malawi Institute of Education  to develop high quality curricular materials sustainably..</narrative>
  </description>
